  "notes": "Measured on the E175 N188SY (left, Nov 2023), checked on N411SY (Feb 2026). SkyWest's E175s for Alaska differ from the mainline in the title: smaller, higher, with 'SkyWest' after it. The right side's 'SkyWest' wasn't seen in these photos, so only the left is drawn (on Horizon's jets the operator name follows the title in reading order, i.e. forward of it on the right). Horizon's own E175s carry 'HORIZON' instead: see regional-horizon. Positions are measured on E175s, whose window line is higher (y about 0.3) than the narrow-body average in COORDINATES.md, so titles placed above or below the windows sit higher than they would on a 737. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N188SY, N411SY (left, from below) and N657QX (right, nearly level), drawn on the E175: the aft sweep had been copied from the 737 and sat about 2 m too far aft as a share of the E175's length; its edges re-measured on the three photos (they agree within about 0.3 m) as smooth curves, with the silver-grey stripe ahead of the lime that the mainline also has. The title placed against the windows: the capital A's top just above the window tops, the baseline about 1.2 m under the windows (y -0.44, cap height 0.66), running 0.11-0.29 on the left and 0.13-0.31 on the right; lowercase about 0.55 of the capital. The fin's art is the 737's as shares of the fin (it looks the same on the E175's photos).",
  "history": "Alaska's regional E175s took the 2016 scheme with the mainline; the operator's name follows the title."
}
